  "description": "The election for Georgia's 12th Congressional District pits incumbent Republican Rep. Rick Allen against a Democratic challenger to be determined by a June 16 primary runoff. Allen, who first won the seat in 2014 by unseating a conservative Democrat, is seeking a sixth term representing the eastern Georgia district that stretches from Augusta to Statesboro. The district has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+7 and is rated 'Solid R' by the Cook Political Report, giving Republicans a structural advantage. Key contrasts in the race center on economic policy, healthcare access, and education funding, with Allen emphasizing his conservative record and business background while Democrats focus on affordability and government accountability.",
